<title>UK: NatWest Markets appoints Lundie as CFO.</title>
<headline>NatWest Markets appoints Lundie as CFO.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>NatWest Markets, the  investment banking arm of National Westminster Bank Plc said on Wednesday it had appointed Tom Lundie as chief financial officer.</p>
<p>Lundie, 49, will report jointly to the banking group's chief financial officer Richard Delbridge and NatWest Markets' chief executive, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Lundie succeeds Mike Ashley who resigned in early February.</p>
